### What changed and why?

| Change | Security / Reliability benefit |
|--------|--------------------------------|
| **`helmet()`** – adds a comprehensive set of HTTP security headers (CSP, HSTS, X‑Frame‑Options, etc.). |
| **Explicit CORS** – only origins you list can access the API. |
| **`express.json({ limit })`** – caps payload size, preventing memory‑exhaustion DoS attacks. |
| **`morgan`** – structured request logs (use a real logger in prod). |
| **Rate limiter** – throttles abusive IPs. |
| **`express-validator`** + `validate` helper – whitelists & sanitises any incoming data. |
| **404 handler** – ensures “not found” is handled consistently. |
| **Central error handler** – logs details server‑side, returns generic error messages to callers (no stack traces in production). |
| **Environment‑driven config** – `PORT`, `NODE_ENV`, `CORS_ORIGIN` come from `.env` (or CI/CD). |
| **Strict typing of query params** – `limit` is coerced to an integer and bounded. |
| **Sanitising email** – `normalizeEmail()` removes dangerous characters. |
| **`createError`** – standardised way to build HTTP errors with proper status codes. |

